WEBVTT

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:22.500
Those Snow White Notes

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.610
Episode 9
Snow Flurries

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.620
<i>Group 20. Umezono Academy of Tokyo.</i>

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.990
<i>So this is the view from
the stage in a competition.</i>

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:50.790
<i>You can see a lot from this side, too.</i>

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:56.550
<i>Even I'm surprised by how calm I'm feeling.</i>

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.050
Handicraft
Club's

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.050
Oscar

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.420
Go, Rai-chan!

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.180
Huh?! High-pitched cheering?

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.680
Rai-chan! Rai-chan! You can do it!

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.670
The squinty guy's the most
popular with the girls?!

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.470
Maybe he's just the most
skilled musician on the team?

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.020
This chair's wobbly...

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.880
Yamazato-san! Maeda-san!

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:21.950
They're so petrified, they aren't
taking in their surroundings.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.420
Let's get started.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.410
Wait.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:29.470
Kaito.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.170
Huh?

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.470
In the first half, strike your
first string as hard as you can.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:37.310
Why just at the beginning?

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:40.800
Your tuning goes out
of whack later. So bluff 'em good!

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.560
Okay! You can do this!

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.280
<i>This tempo...</i>

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:53.400
<i>Sensei told us not to get distracted by
the sound from the speakers, but...</i>

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.890
<i>...it's not a problem.</i>

00:02:55.470 --> 00:03:01.150
<i>All I hear from the speakers is Sawamura-kun's
sound, as if it's been plucked out of the air.</i>

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:04.000
<i>Sawamura Setsu!</i>

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.330
<i>In a team full of strong members,
I gave an amazing performance.</i>

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:14.000
<i>What kind of performance do you think </i>you<i>
can produce, surrounded by these rookies?</i>

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:17.260
<i>Kaito!</i>

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.680
<i>I'll hammer this first string... to bluff them!</i>

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:31.820
<i>What </i>is<i> this?</i>

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.730
<i>It's really singing!</i>

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.040
<i>One person's sound is standing
out more than the rest,</i>

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.690
<i>but it's totally different from the way
Tanuma Mai's sound sang out!</i>

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:46.450
<i>What is this... </i>suppleness<i> in this sound?</i>

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.920
That guy in the middle
has a really nice shamisen.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.670
It's got a great sound.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:55.830
Yeah, it has a good sound, but that's
not the only sound you're hearing.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:56.420
Huh?

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.290
There's another slightly softer
sound overlaid on top of it,

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.890
acting as a cushion.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:06.120
<i>This sound... It must be
one of Kousuke's shamisens.</i>

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.500
<i>He isn't getting it to sing
like Kousuke would, of course,</i>

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.560
<i>but getting this much
out of it is pretty good.</i>

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.360
<i>Still...</i>

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.980
<i>Sawamura's sound...</i>

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:20.490
<i>It's resonating even longer and
more finely than the other guy's.</i>

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:23.220
<i>And the harmony between those sounds...</i>

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.870
<i>That's my friend for you!</i>

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.530
<i>Kaito, that sound is insane!</i>

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.540
<i>The tempo's going to speed up.
I won't fall behind!</i>

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:39.200
<i>The muddiness in Yui's sound is clearing up.</i>

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.270
<i>Maeda-san's fingering is a tiny bit off,
but she's keeping up with the speed.</i>

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.200
<i>This is the best Kaito's ever played.</i>

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.260
<i>Rai-senpai's sound is smooth and fluid.</i>

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:53.540
Is he that "Sawamura Setsu"
guy you were talking about?

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:57.150
He's not really standing out.
Seems pretty average to me.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.560
<i>Sawamura Setsu! Why are
you hiding in the shadows?</i>

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.160
<i>I showed you everything I have!</i>

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.000
I wonder what it is...

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.400
It's kinda ordinary, isn't it?

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.450
Yeah, they're <i>good</i> in a
conventional kind of way, but...

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:15.950
Somehow, they sound better than
any of the teams before them.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.960
<i>It's time to get started, Sawamura!</i>

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:21.110
Nagauta-style techniques?

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.120
Yeah.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:26.460
I want you to add in scattered snow or
cherry blossom petals fluttering down.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.180
Fluttering?

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.620
Just before the high-pitched bit
that goes "tat-tara tat-tara."

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.870
I'll match what you do, Rai-senpai.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.400
You say that like it's super easy.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:42.760
What if I said it would be difficult?

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.100
I won't let you.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.110
Your skills are sound.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.370
Weave it in.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:52.210
<i>If this ends up giving off a
melancholy image, I apologize.</i>

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:53.990
<i>Rai-senpai...</i>

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.210
<i>Go!</i>

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.480
<i>I like fun things!</i>

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.380
Wh-What?

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.890
Osatsuma-bushi!

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:11.820
Huh?

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:15.870
It's an embellishment Osatsuma used.
It's a nagauta-style technique.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:18.270
It was first used for
traditional puppet plays,

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:21.230
before being absorbed into the
nagauta style in the Edo period,

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.890
and even now, it is still
used in kabuki productions.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:28.160
Adding nagauta techniques
into their performance...

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.570
What an unexpected delight!

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.830
<i>This is fun!</i>

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:34.320
<i>I'm enjoying this!</i>

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:35.950
<i>It's so easy to play!</i>

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:43.600
They're clapping before the end.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:47.460
I-It's just an unusual performance.
It's not like they're <i>amazing</i>...

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:50.160
This is a lot of fun!

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.330
Yeah. He's supporting them perfectly.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:56.400
Y-Yeah. He's matching everyone
better than I thought he would.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:00.480
Although... I know this is
exactly what I was hoping for,

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.990
but that just makes it
annoying in its own way.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.090
Setsu, let everyone hear
how amazing you are!

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:08.740
How much of a doting big brother are you?

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:11.790
<i>What are you doing, Setsu?</i>

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.690
<i>This isn't Matsugorou's sound!</i>

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:19.710
<i>I thought what made Jongara interesting
was its tempo and intensity...</i>

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:22.680
<i>I had no idea it could be this playful!</i>

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:25.000
<i>Is there no end to the
creativity on display here?!</i>

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.560
<i>Well done.</i>

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.720
<i>That's Rai-senpai for you.</i>

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:39.020
<i>Kaito nailed it, too. He's making that
quirky shamisen of Seiryuu's sing.</i>

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:43.130
<i>Yui, you haven't made any mistakes.</i>

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:45.910
<i>You're a good kid, and strong when it counts.</i>

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:50.110
<i>Maeda-san, you're keeping tempo perfectly.</i>

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:51.650
<i>Keep it up to the very end.</i>

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:01.970
<i>I'm not thinking about how all
this might turn out. I just...</i>

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.460
Don't you feel like we've
got nothing to fear now?

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.500
I'm starting to feel like we
might actually be able to win!

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.670
I'm so glad...

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:16.010
<i>I thought we should forget
rivaling the other teams...</i>

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:20.390
<i>...because we'd never get
close to matching them.</i>

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:36.330
<i>Guys, just play the way you always do.</i>

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.800
<i>This sound only exists because
of all our sounds combined!</i>

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.320
<i>That's right.</i>

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:09.730
<i>The sound of firm, dry wood thrills
and enchants all the way to your core.</i>

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.460
<i>Huh? Snow?</i>

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.720
<i>No... a flurry of snowflakes.</i>

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.480
Did he... just add in a new sound?

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.020
He did, didn't he?

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.760
I didn't hear anything.

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.280
Ah, yeah, he's the one playing it.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.510
Yes, he's playing it.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:43.160
But why...

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:46.270
How is it so...

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.210
...quiet?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.500
Wow!

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.500
That was amazing!

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.100
This can't be real...

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.320
Seriously?

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:20.520
Th-They're not just being polite, right?

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:30.650
You really did come here
motivated to win, didn't you?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.610
I told you I wanted to win.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.970
You really don't trust me, do you?

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:36.820
Of course I trust you.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:42.880
Thank you!

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:45.330
Welcome to the world of competitions.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.630
Man, I'm exhausted.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:57.020
<i>At this rate, there'll have been no
point in calling it the Matsugorou Cup.</i>

00:10:57.020 --> 00:11:00.540
<i>He seriously won't understand unless
I spell it out, will he? That moron!</i>

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:07.240
We did it! We really did it!

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:09.840
It was amazing! We were amazing!

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.640
Ah, I'm on such a post-performance high!

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.440
Look! I've got goosebumps!

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:18.480
And you two did great!
You didn't lose the tempo once!

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:21.400
I heard Sawamura's sound
through the speakers.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:24.000
That's how I could make sure
I wasn't too fast or too slow.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:27.480
Oh, I did, too! What was
with that, anyway? It's so strange.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:31.470
Well, what <i>I</i> heard was
you guys missing the strings.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:32.670
Is this really the time?

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:36.410
Sawamura said he'd adjust
to us and he did just that.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.260
I hate to admit it,

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.260
but that guy's something else.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:43.260
<i>I'm drenched in sweat.</i>

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.560
<i>To make people hear what you're playing...</i>

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:48.190
<i>takes an insane amount of power.</i>

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:55.230
Making this judgment is draining, isn't it?

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:08.140
<i>Maimai's staring at Sawamura!</i>

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:11.500
<i>And Sawamura has noticed!
They lock eyes!</i>

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:14.420
<i>They must really be a couple!</i>

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:18.080
That girl has been looking for
Sawamura this whole time.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.690
So why's she just glaring at him?

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:21.300
Must be some special circumstances.

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:26.640
Oh. She just glared and left.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:28.100
Mai.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:32.890
Your shamisen... was really stimulating.
You got me all excited.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.890
<i>Stimulating?! Excited?!</i>

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:46.030
You ran away from Aomori.
Nothing you say will make up for that.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:48.790
You're just like old Matsu.
He had no hunger, either.

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:51.310
I take after my dad. I want it all.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:54.800
That difference will show in
the results of this competition.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:06.050
<i>What is everyone trying to gain
by choosing winners and losers?</i>

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:07.850
Um, excuse me...

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:10.640
<i>Wasn't he on the team from Osaka?</i>

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.140
That was amazing! It was <i>crazy</i> good!

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:14.560
Huh? Oh.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.010
It was stupendous!

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:17.530
Well, uh, thanks...

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:19.510
I just <i>had</i> to come tell you how I felt.

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:21.160
I see. Thanks.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:22.780
Okay, later!

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.000
What was that about?

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.710
That's the first time I've seen a guy
play the goody two-shoes card.

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:32.700
But those boyish,
puppy-dog types are so <i>adorbs</i>!

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:33.570
Hey!

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:37.580
Are you in tomorrow's
individual competition?

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:39.040
I am.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.600
You are, huh?

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:45.420
I'm Arakawa Ushio, a third-year from Fukuoka!

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.810
I started playing the
futozao back in sixth grade.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:51.050
I won the junior division of the Kyuushuu
Tournament, achieved A-level ranking,

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:53.100
and I'm performing in
the individual competition!

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:55.230
Remember that!

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:56.360
See you around!

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.110
What was that?

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:06.320
<i>That was the final performance
of the group competition.</i>

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:13.960
<i>The results announcement and the
awards ceremony will begin at 4:10 pm.</i>

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:13.280
Nii-chan. Nii-chan!

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.290
Nii-chan!

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.250
Don't sleep! You're drooling!

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.050
Tell me what you thought.

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.210
What I thought?

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.050
Yes.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:23.680
What did you think, Mother?

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:24.860
You were good.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:27.210
Not that. Do you think we can win?

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:30.010
Only the judges know that. Right?

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.870
What about you, Nii-chan? How was it?

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:36.720
You guys were like WataPachi
popping cotton candy.

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:39.640
Wata

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:39.640
Pachi

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:39.640
Pop Pop Fluff Fluff

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:39.640
Umezono Academy was
like a Super Big Choco bar.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.640
CHOCO

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.820
That kind of comparison...

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.650
...isn't helpful!

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.110
<i>Thank you for your patience.</i>

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:51.870
<i>We will now begin announcing the results,
followed by the awards ceremony.</i>

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:58.220
Umemaru presents the first annual National
High School Tsugaru Shamisen Koshien:

00:14:58.220 --> 00:14:59.740
The Matsugorou Cup.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:02.880
Today, on the first day of the Cup,
we held the group competition.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.880
We have seen all twenty-two
participating groups perform.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:10.240
I will now announce the top six teams,
who will each receive an award.

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:12.380
In sixth place...

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:14.980
From Hokkaido: Shivering.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.360
We did it! Yes!

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:23.170
In fifth place...

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.820
From Fukuoka: Touhou Academy's
Japanese Instrument Club.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:28.720
We did it!

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:32.110
Huh? What?! Fifth?
What do they mean, fifth?!

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:33.870
But we placed! You should be happy!

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:36.730
Why would I be happy?! This isn't right!

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:38.130
I was better than that, right?!

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:40.130
In fourth place...

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:43.760
From Aichi Prefecture:
Yokota Academy's Team AYG.

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.880
For real? I can't believe it!

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:49.850
I'm the one who can't believe it!

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:50.890
Ushio!

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:54.820
No way... Does this mean we didn't place?

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.140
That's not happening! Stay confident!

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:00.570
In third place...

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:01.890
Matsugorou Cup

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:01.890
Presented by Umemaru

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:06.080
From Tokyo: the Umezono Academy!

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.200
Third...

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.060
Wow! We did it!

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:17.790
Third! We placed!

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:21.290
Wh-What's wrong? What is it?

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.230
Third? Why?

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.370
Mai, sit down.

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:32.860
<i>Huh. Third is surprising in its own way.</i>

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:35.380
<i>I guess they were scoring
in the most standard way.</i>

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:39.400
<i>With that performance?
Even if they didn't win, third is...</i>

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:42.460
<i>Which means there's
going to be a major upset.</i>

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:46.400
<i>The wind will be at the eye of the storm.</i>

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.480
In second place...

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.980
From Aomori Prefecture:
Aoba Daiichi High School's

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.120
Maimai and her Fantastic Friends!

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:04.000
Maimai's team is second?

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:08.170
What? What's going on here? Whose
performance could be better than <i>theirs</i>?

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.300
I have no idea.

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.440
<i>Why...</i>

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:13.870
<i>Why?</i>

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:18.700
And the Matsugorou Award
goes to the first place team:

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:19.640
Osaka Prefecture's...

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.140
Billiken-san!

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:22.870
What?

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:25.310
Did he...

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.760
...just say us?

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:31.150
Kaji-kun! They're saying we won!

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.810
WhaвЂ” Really?

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:34.040
For real!

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.280
Hey, sir! Say it again!

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:39.530
The Matsugorou Award goes to
Osaka Prefecture's Billiken-san!

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:44.920
We... did it!

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.490
Yeah!

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:50.920
<i>How did I lose in a
tournament full of amateurs?</i>

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:54.480
<i>Beating Sawamura was
my goal here, but still...</i>

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:59.200
<i>I hate this... I hate that I'm not first.</i>

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:02.480
We will now begin the awards ceremony.

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:05.560
Please can the teams that
placed come up onto the stage.

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.430
Mai, come on, let's go.

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:11.900
I don't accept this! I'm not going
up there! I'm staying right here!

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:14.430
H-How could I have lost?

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:15.080
Mai.

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:18.910
You didn't hear Osaka's performance.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.700
Don't disgrace yourself.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:24.570
You put too much trust in your own
abilities and this is what happened.

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:28.620
Your sound wasn't kind on the ears.

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:31.200
You're not playing the shamisen for fun.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:33.290
Accept their assessment.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.800
1st Annual National High School

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.800
Tsugaru Shamisen Koshien

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.800
Matsugorou Cup

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:39.800
But man, what a surprise.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:44.440
Everyone in Mai's team
placed in junior competitions.

00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:46.780
I bet no one expected a
competition as insane as this.

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:49.470
Osaka produced a perfect
ensemble performance.

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:52.820
The fact they didn't have
any minuses is scary in itself.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:59.320
Fukuoka was good, but they weren't together.
The grandstanding stood out the most.

00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:03.830
Aichi wasn't particularly good,
but they were really together.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.580
It was probably super close
between the top three.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.970
Rai-chan!

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:12.390
<i>Setsu and the others harmonized well,</i>

00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:15.090
<i>but they weren't as good as Mai's
group of high-level musicians.</i>

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:18.030
<i>Mai's sound was outstanding
and really stood out.</i>

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:21.840
<i>The difference from Fukuoka was
that her group was all high-level,</i>

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.010
<i>and their sounds clashed.</i>

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:27.850
<i>With Osaka, all their
strengths meshed together.</i>

00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:31.060
<i>Like they were giving a primer
on how to play in an ensemble.</i>

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:35.280
<i>All the judges gave them high
scores, without exception.</i>

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:39.190
<i>And there wasn't anything
to mark them down on. Still...</i>

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:41.570
<i>This isn't any fun.</i>

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.210
Congratulations.

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:44.950
Thank you very much!

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:47.320
<i>Still...</i>

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:51.310
<i>He's just so cute!</i>

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:53.420
<i>He's like a little puppy!</i>

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:56.540
It was a very close race
between the top three teams.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.500
Any one of them could have won
without it coming as a shock.

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:03.120
The teams that performed today
all had their own personalities...

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:04.810
<i>First place... Did we ever
really have a chance?</i>

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:07.980
<i>Getting ranked is really exhausting.</i>

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:12.940
<i>The sound we made together today...</i>

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:15.360
<i>I loved it!</i>

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:18.380
And now, onto our last
announcement for the group division!

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:22.470
They wowed the audience more than any other
group, showed us the potential of sound,

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.470
and excited us all!

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:27.190
The Judges' Special Award goes to:

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:29.880
Tokyo Metropolis's Umezono Academy!

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:39.920
Of course it would!
Of course it does! Yay! Yay!

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:43.690
C'mon, c'mon.

00:20:43.690 --> 00:20:44.510
Go get it!

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:55.450
You did incredibly well. I was really moved.

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:57.290
Th-Thank you.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:15.870
<i>Did I...</i>

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:22.960
<i>...really beat Sawamura Setsu?</i>

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:28.340
If someone plays a sound you don't
have inside yourself, it electrifies you,

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:30.180
but it also fills you with jealousy.

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:33.860
That sensation is so painful, so ugly...

00:21:33.860 --> 00:21:35.730
It's a terrible thing.

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:37.590
<i>When will you...</i>

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:40.860
<i>...learn what it means to suffer?</i>

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:51.630
That's what you call a close race.

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:55.050
It's... so frustrating...

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:57.960
But you got third, and you
only started in the spring!

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.020
I think that's really amazing!

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:01.740
Right, Oodawara-sensei?

00:22:01.740 --> 00:22:04.240
Yes! I-I'm moved and impressed!

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:06.010
You guys were the best!

00:22:06.350 --> 00:22:08.880
But... I'm still upset.

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:12.010
Me, too. I'm devastated.

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:21.160
<i>I didn't know... I...</i>

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:24.780
<i>I didn't realize how much
I didn't want to lose.</i>

00:22:28.770 --> 00:22:30.990
<i>Enough to make me feel this bad.</i>

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:33.760
<i>That's how amazing our performance was.</i>

00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:39.180
<i>I did everything I could. I have no regrets.</i>

00:22:40.070 --> 00:22:41.180
<i>But...</i>

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:45.160
<i>My chest feels tight.</i>

00:22:55.190 --> 00:22:59.470
So those two have heard each
other perform for the first time.

00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:04.530
I wonder what kind of
performance he'll give.

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:06.520
My friend, I mean.

00:23:08.410 --> 00:23:10.780
<i>Nothing shakes him, huh?</i>

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:15.160
Tanukichi Diner

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:18.660
Matsugorou Cup

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:18.660
It's a shame Mai isn't
going to be in it, but...

00:23:18.660 --> 00:23:21.730
That Kaji-kun guy from
Osaka was pretty good.

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:24.090
I wonder how he'll do in the individuals.

00:23:24.090 --> 00:23:25.910
Oh, and the Fukuoka Pwing

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:27.440
It's "Arakawa Twang."

00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:29.180
Oh, right. The Arakawa Twang.

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:31.530
They were good.

00:23:31.530 --> 00:23:33.310
Quit saying useless things.

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:36.560
Your competition is Souichi. Just him.

00:23:40.190 --> 00:23:41.410
Setsu-san?

00:23:43.880 --> 00:23:47.250
Dad... I mean, my father said
to help yourselves to these.

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:47.230
What's the difference between
a "twang" and a "pwing"?

00:23:47.220 --> 00:23:54.730
I mean it really wasn't a twang.
It seemed more like a "pwing."

00:23:47.250 --> 00:23:50.750
Thanks, but even if they look it,
they're not old enough to drink.

00:23:50.750 --> 00:23:52.810
Ah, I'm sorry.

00:23:52.810 --> 00:23:55.000
Well then, good night.

00:23:54.730 --> 00:23:56.760
Which is better, a "twang" or a "pwing"?

00:23:55.410 --> 00:23:58.330
You're always doing so much for me. Thanks.

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:59.000
Which is better? Between
a "twang" or a "pwing"?

00:24:02.620 --> 00:24:04.760
Good luck on the individuals.
